extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 61-63 (cache p062-p064, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order, with the stat block on printed 62 checked against a render. Heading Guide O.C.C. on printed 61; the stat block is headed Aboriginal Wilderness Guide O.C.C. on printed 62 and runs to printed 63. || ONE CLASS, NOT A VARIANT: the Outback list on printed 56 calls it Guide or Wilderness Scout O.C.C., the entry is titled Guide O.C.C., and the Aboriginal Wilderness Guide heading is the heading of its only stat block; the lore says Wilderness Guides are Aboriginals. No second set of figures is printed. The stat-block heading is used as the name because the catalog already holds other guides and scouts. || RACE: the Special O.C.C. Bonus note says to roll attributes and add the bonuses for race in the section on making up Aboriginal characters; this book has no such section (printed 87 and 193 defer Aboriginal characters to Rifts Australia Two) and the catalog has no Aboriginal race, so the race is a restriction in prose and no race bonus is stored. || GROUP: listed under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56; the entry states no S.D.C. base, only +4D6+10 to S.D.C., so men_of_arms is false and occ_group is optional. || XP: the Raider, Technologist, Guide/Scout/Hunter & Bushman ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || BONUSES: +4D6+10 S.D.C., +1D6 Spd, +1 P.P., +1 initiative, +1 roll with punch, fall or impact stored. || SKILL READINGS: Speaks English is Language: Australian English; Tracking is Tracking (people); Track Animals is the catalog row Track & Trap Animals (20/5); General Athletics is Athletics (general); W.P. Spear & Woomera is W.P. Spear. Dance (+10%), or Corroboree at no bonus, is a pick of two with no bonus stored, because one bonus per group cannot differ by option; Dance is 10% short and the note says so. Play Musical Instrument: (+5%) is printed with the instrument blank (render); the catalog row Play Musical Instrument is used, not Play Aboriginal Musical Instrument. The book prints a bare Use (+10%) between Blend and W.P. Boomerang (render); it is read as Use Songlines, the only skill of that name in the book. Blend is stored at the catalog base plus the printed +10%; the Blend description on printed 159 gives all Aboriginal characters a further +10% that is NOT added. || RELATED: three at level one, one more at levels 2, 5, 8, 12 and 15. Cowboy only Herding Cattle, Lore: Cattle and Whittling: Lore: Cattle is Lore: Cattle & Animals; Whittling is the catalog Technical row Whittling & Sculpting, reachable through Technical at +5%, not listed under Cowboy. Mechanical Basic only is Basic Mechanics. Pick Locks and Pick Pockets are filed under Espionage in the catalog and named in the Rogue only-list at the Rogue +10% (Espionage is also +10%). Pilot except Robot Elite, Power Armor and military vehicles excludes the robot, power armor and military rows. The book files Horsemanship under Pilot (printed 151-152); the catalog category is offered as General and Exotic Animals. Electrical and Pilot Related are none. || SECONDARY: two at levels 1, 4, 8 and 12. || MONEY: 2D6x$100 in dollars; Australian dollars equal credits. || EQUIPMENT: only the boomerang and spear are stated outright and stored (boomerang type is not printed; the average row is used). NOT stored: the outfit is the player choice of a loincloth or Jackaroo-style dress with light homespun M.D.C. armor (never full environmental), boots, utility belt, backpack and canteen; personal items; snakebite drugs and binoculars (the book says the Guide can see the sense in them); and, depending on skills, an Aboriginal blowgun or crossbow and one M.D. weapon. They are in GM Notes."
---

## Lore

The Guide is an Aboriginal who walks with the white man: rather than stay
with the tribe, he lives and works in an Outbacker community and offers it his
knowledge of the land. The role is centuries old and had nearly died out
before the Rifts. It is common again, and now the Guide is adviser and
philosopher as well as scout and go-between. Almost every Outback settlement
has one or two and counts them a great asset.

It can be a divided life. Some tribes see living among Outbackers as weakness
and shun those who do it. Others have found a balance, initiated as warriors
of their tribe and still welcome in town as fellow Outbackers, and that is
becoming more usual as the years pass.

A Guide can live in the bush indefinitely, fights well and knows a good deal
about many things, with a firmer spiritual footing than a Jackaroo. He is not
quite the bushman a traditional Aboriginal is, and one day he may have to
choose between his two worlds.

## GM Notes

This is one class with one stat block. The book titles the entry Guide O.C.C.,
lists it as Guide or Wilderness Scout, and heads the statistics Aboriginal
Wilderness Guide O.C.C.

Race: the book tells the player to roll attributes and add the racial bonuses
from its section on making up Aboriginal characters, but that section is not
in this book; it is deferred to Rifts Australia Two.

Skill adjustments the sheet does not make: Dance is +10% if taken instead of
Corroboree; Blend gains a further +10% for an Aboriginal character (printed
159); the instrument for Play Musical Instrument is the player''s choice. The
book prints the songline skill only as Use (+10%).

Starting kit beyond the boomerang and spear is the player''s call: a simple
loincloth, or Outbacker dress with light homespun M.D.C. armor (never full
environmental), boots, utility belt, backpack and canteen; a few items of
personal significance (face paint, a luck fetish, a small silver cross, a
photograph); perhaps snakebite drugs and binoculars. Depending on skills, an
Aboriginal blowgun or crossbow and one M.D. weapon.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'guide-australia');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'guide-australia';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-guide-australia-class.sql');
